<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<!DOCTYPE topic SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/html-entities.dtd">

<topic 
	xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" 
	xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
	title="Organizations" id="cloud-organizations">

    <show-structure for="chapter" depth="3"/>

    <link-summary>Organizations provide top-level structuring of all entities in %cloud%. Every organization is
        created on the basis of a specific JetBrains account.</link-summary>

    <p>Organizations provide top-level structuring of all entities in <a href="https://qodana.cloud">%cloud%</a>.
    Every organization is created on the basis of a specific JetBrains account. Depending on your choice, it will be either
        private or public.
        Every account in %cloud% is based on the organization that becomes its default organization.
    </p>

    <p>You can navigate between organizations using the list in the upper left part of the %cloud% UI.</p>

    <img src="qc-settings-organization-navigate-between.gif" width="706" alt="Creating an organization" border-effect="line"/>

    <chapter id="cloud-organizations-create-organization" title="Create an organization">

        <p>You can create private or public organizations. Reports stored in private organizations are accessible only
            by a user who created an organization and users who were invited to them.
            Reports stored in public organizations are available for all %cloud% users, including unauthorized users with the
            <a href="cloud-user-roles.md">viewer role</a>. </p>

        <p>Each organization is created on the basis of a specific <a href="cloud-get-access.topic">JetBrains account</a>.</p>

        <procedure>
            <step>
                <p>In the sidebar, expand the list of organizations and then click
                    <ui-path>Create organization</ui-path>.</p>

                <img src="qc-settings-organization-create.png" dark-src="qc-settings-organization-create_dark.png" width="706" alt="Creating an organization" border-effect="line"/>
            </step>
            <step>
                <p>Complete the project setup stage. You can read more about this stage in the <a href="set-up-your-project.md"/> section.</p>
            </step>
        </procedure>
    </chapter>

    <chapter id="cloud-organizations-overview" title="Configure organizations">

        <link-summary>You can configure membership and visibility of your organization, or leave the organization.</link-summary>

        <p>You can configure membership and visibility of your organization, or leave the organization.</p>

        <procedure>

            <step>
                <p>In the sidebar, navigate to the organization that you wish to configure. </p>
                <img src="qc-settings-organization-navigate-between.gif" width="706" alt="Creating an organization" border-effect="line"/>
            </step>
            <step>
                <p>On the organization page, click the <ui-path>Organization settings</ui-path> button in the upper-right corner.</p>
                <img src="qc-settings-organization-manage-access.png" dark-src="qc-settings-organization-manage-access_dark.png" width="706" alt="Navigate to the organization settings" border-effect="line"/>
            </step>

        </procedure>

        <p>Click the button in the upper-right corner of the UI to switch the status of your organization, rename it, leave it, or completely delete it.</p>

        <img src="qc-settings-organization-leave-temp.png" width="706" alt="Managing an organization" border-effect="line"/>

        <note>You cannot leave or delete an organization in case you are the only member of it, so you need to assign a new
            administrator beforehand.</note>


        <p>On the settings page, you can find the following tabs:</p>

        <list>
            <li><a anchor="cloud-organizations-subscription"><ui-path>Subscription</ui-path></a> contains the %instance% license information.</li>
            <li><a anchor="cloud-organizations-logs"><ui-path>Logs</ui-path></a> provides a list of log entries for a specific time interval.</li>
            <li><a anchor="cloud-organizations-invitation"><ui-path>Members</ui-path></a> lets you manage organization members.</li>
            <li><a anchor="cloud-organization-sso"><ui-path>SSO</ui-path></a> lets you configure the <a href="cloud-sso.md">Single Sign-on functionality</a> for %cloud%.</li>
            <li><a anchor="cloud-organizations-api-token"><ui-path>API token</ui-path></a> lets you generate and manage a permanent organization token used by the <a href="cloud-api.md">public API</a> of %cloud%.
                This feature is available only under the <a href="pricing.md">Ultimate Plus license</a> and only for %cloud% users of the <code>Owner</code> and <code>Admin</code> <a href="cloud-user-roles.md">roles</a>.</li>
            <li><a anchor="cloud-organizations-global-configurations"><ui-path>Global configurations</ui-path></a> let you manage <a href="global-configuration.md">configurations used across many projects</a> of your organization.</li>
        </list>

        <chapter id="cloud-organizations-subscription" title="Subscription">

            <p>Using the <ui-path>Subscription</ui-path> tab, you can see information about your %product% license.</p>

            <img src="qc-settings-subscription.png" width="706" alt="The Subscription tab of %cloud%" border-effect="line"/>

        </chapter>

        <chapter id="cloud-organizations-logs" title="Logs">

            <p>Using the <ui-path>Logs</ui-path> tab, you can view %cloud% log entries for a specific time interval.</p>

            <img src="qc-settings-logs.png" width="706" alt="The Logs tab of %cloud%" border-effect="line"/>

        </chapter>

        <chapter id="cloud-organizations-invitation" title="Members">

            <link-summary>Explore how you can manage membership in your %cloud% organization.</link-summary>

            <p>Using the <ui-path>Members</ui-path> tab, you can:</p>

            <list>
                <li>Invite new members to your organization using email addresses, and assign them <a href="cloud-user-roles.md">user roles</a>.</li>
                <li>Change <a href="cloud-user-roles.md">the roles</a> of the existing organization members.</li>
                <li>Exclude members from your organization.</li>
            </list>

            <note>Members created and configured through <a href="cloud-sso.md">JetBrains Hub</a> cannot be modified or deleted in %cloud% UI.</note>

            <procedure>
                <step>
                    <p>On the <a anchor="cloud-organizations-overview">settings page</a> of the organization, navigate
                        to the <ui-path>Members</ui-path> tab.</p>
                </step>
                <step>
                    <p>On the <ui-path>Members</ui-path> tab, click <ui-path>Invite members</ui-path>.</p>
                    <img src="qc-settings-organization-invite-members.png" width="706" alt="Clicking the Invite members button" border-effect="line"/>

                </step>
                <step>
                    <p>On the <ui-path>Invite members to ...</ui-path> dialog that opens, you can manage members of your organization.</p>
                    <img src="qc-settings-organization-manage-members.png" dark-src="qc-settings-organization-manage-members.png" width="706" alt="Managing organization membership" border-effect="line"/>
                </step>
            </procedure>
        </chapter>

        <chapter id="cloud-organization-sso" title="SSO">

            <p>Using the <ui-path>SSO</ui-path> tab, you can set up subdomains employed by third-party identity providers for
                authentication in %cloud% and %premlite%. The details are available in the <a href="cloud-sso.md"/> section.</p>

            <note>
                This functionality is visible only for users under Ultimate Plus <a href="pricing.md">licenses</a>
                purchased for a minimum of ten users.
            </note>

            <note>This tab is visible only if your %cloud% user has either the <code>Owner</code> or <code>Admin</code>
                <a href="cloud-user-roles.md" anchor="cloud-user-org-roles-owner">role</a> in %cloud% or %premlite%.</note>

            <procedure>
                <step>
                    <p>On the <ui-path>SSO</ui-path> tab, enter the name of the subdomain that you would like to use for authentication, and then
                        click the <ui-path>Generate URL</ui-path> button.</p>
                    <img src="qc-settings-sso.png" width="706" alt="The SSO tab of the organization settings" border-effect="line"/>
                </step>
                <step>
                    <p>On this tab, copy the URL and follow the recommendations.</p>
                    <img src="qc-settings-sso-2.png" width="706" alt="The second step of the SSO subdomain generation" border-effect="line"/>
                </step>
            </procedure>


        </chapter>

        <chapter id="cloud-organizations-api-token" title="API token">

            <link-summary>Using the API token tab, you can have access to the Public API to create teams, projects, and
                obtain a list of users in %cloud% and %premlite% using your build pipelines.</link-summary>

            <note>This tab is visible only if your %cloud% user has either the <code>Owner</code> or <code>Admin</code>
                <a href="cloud-user-roles.md" anchor="cloud-user-org-roles-owner">role</a> in %cloud% or %premlite%.</note>

            <note>
                This tab is visible only for users under the Ultimate Plus <a href="pricing.md">license</a>.
            </note>

            <p>Using the <ui-path>API token</ui-path> tab, you can generate and manage an organization API token. This token lets you
            have access to the <a href="cloud-api.md">Public API</a> to create <a href="cloud-teams.topic">teams</a>,
            <a href="cloud-projects.topic">projects</a>, and obtain a list of %cloud% and %premlite% organization users
            using your <a href="ci.md">build pipelines</a>.</p>

            <img src="qc-settings-organization-api-token.png" width="706" alt="The API token tab" border-effect="line"/>
        </chapter>

        <chapter id="cloud-organizations-global-configurations" title="Global configurations">

            <note>
                This tab is visible only for users under the Ultimate Plus <a href="pricing.md">license</a>.
            </note>

            <p>Using the <ui-path>Global configurations</ui-path> tab, you can manage <a href="global-configuration.md">global configurations</a>. Here,
                you can find the list of configurations that can be used across multiple projects of your organization.
                For each configuration, you can view projects connected to it, the configuration description, and the
                time of the latest update.</p>

            <p>Using the list of projects, you can:</p>
            <list>
                <li>View linked projects</li>
                <li>Check usage statistics</li>
                <li>Search for projects analyzed using the configuration</li>
                <li>Assign or view global configurations for specific projects</li>
            </list>

            <p>Here, you can also modify the list of projects that use the specific global configuration.</p>

            <p>This procedure explains how you can create your global configuration:</p>
            <chapter id="cloud-organizations-global-configurations-connect-a-repository" title="Connect a repository">
                <procedure>
                    <step>
                        <p>On the <ui-path>Global configurations</ui-path> tab, click the <ui-path>Connect repository</ui-path> button.</p>
                        <img src="gpc-global-configuration-tab.png" thumbnail="true" alt="The Global configuration tab" width="940" border-effect="line"/>
                    </step>
                    <step>On the page that opens, select your CI/CD tool and follow the instructions about a
                        <a href="global-configuration.md" anchor="Uploading+to+Qodana+Cloud">configuration token</a>.</step>
                    <img src="gpc-onboarding-cicd.png" alt="Configuring a CI/CD solution" width="710" border-effect="line"/>
                    <step>Also on that page, follow the instructions to configure a job.</step>
                    <img src="gpc-onboarding-cicd-2.png" alt="Configuring a CI/CD solution" width="710" border-effect="line"/>
                </procedure>

                <p>Once the first run of a CI/CD solution with the uploader is complete, the global configuration is uploaded
                    and becomes visible on the <ui-path>Global configurations</ui-path> tab.</p>

                <img src="global-configuration-overview.png" width="1236" alt="Overview of global configurations" border-effect="line"/>

                <chapter id="cloud-organizations-global-configurations-modify-global-configuration" title="Modify a global configuration">
                    <p>Click the configuration that you would like to modify. This will open the page containing all
                        configuration parameters. On this page, you can view the files that define the global configuration
                        and obtain a link to the VCS to be able to edit its files. </p>
                    <img src="modify-global-configuration.png" alt="Global configuration components" width="1051" border-effect="line"/>
                </chapter>

                <chapter id="cloud-organizations-global-configurations-view-modify-list-of-projects" title="View and modify the list of projects">
                    <p>Click the <ui-path>Edit projects list</ui-path> button to open a dialog containing the list
                        of projects.</p>
                    <img src="gpc-project-list.png" width="1280" alt="Projects connected with a global configuration" border-effect="line"/>

                    <p>On the <ui-path>Connected Projects</ui-path> dialog you can view, assign, and unassign configurations.
                        You can also see whether the project is already assigned to another global configuration, and
                        you’ll get a warning if you try to override it. Besides that, it shows information about the latest
                        analysis. To be redirected to the analysis report, click a specific project name.</p>

                    <!-- Image of projects is required here -->
                </chapter>

            </chapter>

            <chapter id="cloud-organizations-global-configurations-revoke-regenerate-token" title="Manage configuration token">
                <p>In case a <a href="global-configuration.md" anchor="Uploading+to+Qodana+Cloud">configuration token</a> is compromised,
                    click the <ui-path>Actions</ui-path> and then click <ui-path>Revoke configuration token</ui-path>
                    to revoke the token and clear all configurations.</p>
                <img src="global-project-actions.png" alt="Actions for a global configuration" width="378" border-effect="line"/>
                <p>On the <ui-path>Revoke configuration token</ui-path> dialog, specify whether you would like to remove all global configurations after revoking the token. </p>
                <img src="gpc-revoke-token-dialog.png" alt="Actions for a global configuration" width="1280" border-effect="line"/>
                <!-- How can a token be regenerated after it has been revoked? -->

            </chapter>


        </chapter>

    </chapter>


</topic>
